{{PRODUCTS}}
HTML,
'en_content'=><<<'HTML'
<p>Buying <strong>extra virgin olive oil from a Spanish olive mill</strong> makes it easier to know who produces the oil, how it is made and which formats are available. At El Mercado de Origen we feature EVOO from <strong>1957</strong>, a family project connected with olive growing for three generations.</p>
<p>The range covers different household needs, from 5-litre containers to cases of 1-litre bottles and 500 ml formats. This lets you choose according to both flavour preference and how you use olive oil at home.</p>
{{PRODUCTS}}
<h2>Extra virgin olive oil from a family mill</h2><p>1957 works with olives harvested from the tree and produces its oils using mechanical methods. Temperature control is a defining part of the process, with cold extraction kept below 19 °C.</p>
<h2>Choosing the right format</h2><p>A <strong>5 L container</strong> is convenient for regular cooking and everyday use. Cases of <strong>1 L bottles</strong> are easy to store and open one at a time, while <strong>500 ml bottles</strong> suit lighter consumption or table use.</p>
<h2>Varieties and flavour profiles</h2><p>The 5 L product is offered in different olive varieties. Arbequina tends to be milder, while Marteño —Picual— and Lechín offer more pronounced profiles. The best choice depends on how you plan to use the oil and the flavours you prefer.</p>
<h2>Buy EVOO with a visible producer</h2><p>Each product keeps the producer visible so you can compare format, price and variety without losing sight of origin.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What does extra virgin mean?</h3><p>Extra virgin is the highest category of virgin olive oil and must meet the applicable chemical and sensory standards.</p><h3>Is a 5 L format practical?</h3><p>It can be ideal for frequent household use, provided the oil is stored sealed, away from light and heat.</p>
{{PRODUCTS}}
HTML
